From 9e4fff00d244a8b5300d03569addd019ec8e262f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Denton <z@chdenton.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:05:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [Loom] Bind dependent types before checking inline boundaries

Compare callee types after mapping argument dimensions and encoding references into the caller. Refine projected types with shared exact facts when ordinary substitution is insufficient; acquire the fact snapshot lazily once per pass and retain it for rewriting. Use the same comparison for cloned and transferred return replacements.

Cover runtime dimensions, multiple static widths, identity and computed vector returns, and template vector arguments through native source-to-low. Validation: 550 available compiler fixture suites pass. Four additional source-low suites have identical pre-existing failures when rebuilding the unchanged parent commit.
